  "body": "## Associated User Story\r\n\r\n[P5-31: Add details to signup](https://pt-502.atlassian.net/browse/P5-31)\r\n\r\nAs a user, I want to also be able to add expected graduation, PT school application (put ‘anticipated application cycle’) - (summers only, for example summer 2026, summer 2027, etc…), show availability for carpooling for field trips, and opt into providing a phone number.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance Criteria\r\n\r\n### Members can add and edit these profile details, and the phone number is only shared if they opt in.\r\n\r\n- Sunny: A member opens their profile and selects an expected graduation term, a PT school application summer (e.g., Summer 2026, Summer 2027), whether they're available to carpool, and optionally checks a box to share their phone number and enters it. They save and see a confirmation. The information appears on their profile, carpool availability is visible to officers when planning field trips, and the phone number is visible only if they opted in.\r\n- Rainy: A member leaves a required field blank, picks a non-summer application term, enters an invalid phone number, or the save fails. The system shows a clear error (e.g., \"Please choose a summer term\" or \"Enter a valid phone number\") instead of failing silently, and their previous information stays in place. If a member has not opted in, their phone number is never shown to others, and only the member and officers can edit their own details.\r\n\r\nDefinition of Done -\r\n\r\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\r\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\r\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\r\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\r\n\r\n## Validation and Setup\r\n\r\nRSpec after updating from main: 329 examples, 0 failures, 1 existing pending example. JavaScript: 8 tests passed. RuboCop passed. See the [PR checks](https://github.com/FA26-CSCE431-software-engineering/PT-502/pull/34/checks) for CI results.\r\n\r\nRun `bin/rails db:migrate` for the two profile migrations. Existing phone data is preserved; phone sharing uses the existing `phone_visible` consent field.\r\n\r\n## Section D: Deferred Items\r\n\r\nNon-author code review and the human maintainability checks are awaiting team review. The existing pending HomeHelper example is unchanged. No new RuboCop exclusions.\r\n",
